Article 22
(1) Forms of services for Victims organized by P2TP2A include:
a. medical services;
b. medico-legal services;
c. psychosocial services;
d. legal services;
e. social reintegration services; and
f. economic independence services.
(2) Provisions regarding the mechanism of services for victims organized by P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated by Mayor Regulation.

CHAPTER VIII
COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION
Article 25
(1) The community may participate in the protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence. (2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out through:
a. provision of safe houses and/or shelters; b. establishment and management of orphanages for children;
c. establishment of child rehabilitation centers;
d. active supervision of violence against women and children and reporting to the competent authorities;
e. providing first aid to victims; f. reporting the occurrence of violence against women and children and providing protection;
g. forming family partners at the village level by the community; and
h. other forms of community participation related to the implementation of protection of women and protection of children.

MAYOR OF BANJAR,

Considering : a. that every woman and child has the right to survival, growth, and proper development as well as the right to protection from violence and discrimination as mandated in the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

b. that acts of violence against women and children in Banjar City have been increasing from year to year so that it becomes the responsibility of the Regional Government of Banjar City to guarantee the protection, fulfillment, and respect for the rights of women and children;

c. that Banjar City does not yet have a regional regulation governing the implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence so that a comprehensive legal basis is needed in order to fulfill the rights of women and children;

d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation on the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence;

In View of : 1. Article 18 Paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as has been amended several times, most recently by Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 1 of 2016 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2016 Number 99, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5882);

3. Law Number 27 of 2002 concerning the Establishment of Banjar City in West Java Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 130, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4246);

4. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);

5. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as has been amended several times most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);

With Mutual Approval

Article 15
(1) Rehabilitation Services for Child Victims of Violence as referred to in Article 11 letter c shall be conducted in the form of: a. legal aid services;
b. health rehabilitation services;
c. social rehabilitation services; and/or
d. repatriation and social reintegration services.
(2) In the Rehabilitation Services for Child Victims of Violence as referred to in paragraph (1), the City Regional Government may cooperate with:
a. vertical agencies;
b. provincial government;
c. other regency/city governments;
d. village government;
e. non-governmental organizations;
f. private parties;
g. community; and/or
h. family.
(3) Further provisions regarding the form and procedures for rehabilitation services for Child Victims of Violence as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated in a Mayor Regulation.

Article 5
The stages of protection for women victims of violence include: a. prevention of violence against women;
b. protection services for women victims of violence; and c. empowerment of women victims of violence.

Article 24
The duties and functions of FPKK as referred to in Article 23 consist of:
a. coordinating and synchronizing prevention, services, and empowerment for women and children victims of violence;
b. maintaining and developing FPKK in prevention, services, and empowerment of victims through networking and referral systems;
c. conducting education on non-discrimination values towards women and children;
d. conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to the implementation of Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence;
e. collecting, compiling, and presenting data reports on victims of violence; and
f. conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence.

