Article 13
Efforts to prevent Violence against Children as referred to in Article 12 shall be carried out by involving:
a. parents and/or family;
b. community;
c. educational institutions;
d. child social welfare institutions; and/or
e. other institutions engaged in the field of child protection care.

Article 6
(1) Prevention of violence against women as referred to in Article 5 letter a shall be carried out in an integrated manner coordinated by the Regional Apparatus responsible for women's empowerment and child protection.
(2) Prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by involving:
a. family;
b. community;
c. private sector;
d. community institutions;
e. social institutions; and
f. educational institutions.

Article 8
(1) Protection Services for Women Victims of Violence as referred to in Article 5 letter b shall be provided to women residents of the Region and/or women who experience violence with the incident location in the Region.
(2) The implementation of Protection Services for Women Victims of Violence as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out with the principles of:
a. swift;
b. safe;
c. empathy;
d. non-discrimination;
e. easily accessible; and
f. guaranteed confidentiality.

Article 5
The stages of protection for women victims of violence include: a. prevention of violence against women;
b. protection services for women victims of violence; and c. empowerment of women victims of violence.

Article 3
Protection of women and children victims of violence is implemented based on the principles of:
a. gender responsiveness;
b. non-discrimination;
c. equal and respectful relationships;
d. maintaining privacy and confidentiality;
e. providing a sense of safety and comfort;
f. respecting individual differences;
g. non-judgmental;
h. respecting the choices and decisions of victims;
i. sensitivity to the background and conditions of victims; j. use of language that is appropriate and understood by victims; k. fast and simple;
l. empathy; and
m. best interests of victims.

